### Issue Analysis

This bug affects MPAv2 apps (`st.navigation` + `st.Page`) whose `url_path` contains non-ASCII characters. Browsers percent-encode these characters in the address bar/history (e.g. `Págé_…` → `P%C3%A1g%C3%A9_…`), so on a Back/Forward (`popstate`) event the path delivered to the frontend is the encoded form while the registered `appPage.urlPathname` is the decoded form. Page lookup then fails and the app silently falls back to the main page.

**Likely root cause:** In `frontend/app/src/util/AppNavigation.ts` (`findPageByUrlPath`), the comparison is a raw string `endsWith` between `document.location.pathname` (encoded) and `appPage.urlPathname` (decoded):

```200:208:frontend/app/src/util/AppNavigation.ts
  findPageByUrlPath(pathname: string): IAppPage | null {
    return (
      this.appPages.find(appPage =>
        // The page name is embedded at the end of the URL path, and if not, we are in the main page.
        // See https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/blob/1.19.0/frontend/src/App.tsx#L740
        pathname.endsWith("/" + appPage.urlPathname)
      ) ?? this.mainPage
    )
  }
```

For comparison, the sibling helper `extractPageNameFromPathName` in `frontend/lib/src/util/utils.ts` already decodes via `decodeURIComponent(...)`, which is why direct/initial navigation to a unicode `url_path` can resolve correctly but Back/Forward restoration does not. The fix is most likely to `decodeURIComponent` the incoming `pathname` (or both sides) before the `endsWith` comparison, with safe handling for malformed sequences.

This handler is wired up via the `popstate` listener registered in `frontend/app/src/App.tsx` (`onHistoryChange`), which explains the Back/Forward-specific symptom.

### Related Issues

- [#10572 — `st.page_link` and `st.switch_page` don't raise errors when pointing to non-existent pages with the same pathname as a real page](https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/issues/10572): Another case where page-path resolution in `st.navigation` is too lenient and silently falls back/redirects instead of resolving (or erroring) on the intended page.
- [#9279 — Query Params not preserved on first script run after using the browser "back" button](https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/issues/9279): Same code path (`popstate`/browser Back handling for multipage apps); demonstrates other state-synchronization issues during browser history restoration.
- [#9878 — Moving slider seems to generate 2 new (empty) window.history states](https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/issues/9878): Related browser-history handling bug in Streamlit's navigation/history integration.

